id: pm-pd7nh0
title: "MCP 2026-07-28 per-request log level is neither read nor negatively controlled, and the conformance matrix has no row for it"
description: "The 2026-07-28 key-changes list (item 5) removes logging/setLevel and sets log level per request through the _meta key io.modelcontextprotocol/logLevel; servers MUST NOT emit notifications/message for requests that did not include the field. The literal appears in zero source files and zero tests. pm never emits notifications/message, so the MUST NOT holds vacuously, but nothing proves it and the conformance matrix in docs/MCP_2026_07_28_CONFORMANCE.md assigns the requirement no owner and no evidence row, which is the one shape the matrix promised not to have.\n\nAcceptance: the request-metadata parser accepts and validates the key against the specification level enum and refuses an invalid level with -32602 while leaving the request otherwise processable; a negative control proves no notifications/message frame is emitted on stdio and Streamable HTTP for a request that omits the key, and that a request carrying the key is accepted unchanged; the matrix gains the row with owner and executable evidence; the generated deprecation inventory and the removed-method controls stay green."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: "area:sdk",conformance,mcp,protocol
